    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481-a2">

                <pb facs="0491" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg415"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Chargé Jay </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to the esteemed note verbale of April 27, 1916, and its <hi
                        rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> of May 1, 1916, the Imperial and Royal
                    Ministry for Foreign Affairs has the honor to request the Embassy of the United
                    States of America to be good enough to inform the Department of State in
                    Washington that the Imperial and Royal Government had pleasure in receiving the
                    assurance that subsequent to his repatriation no passport enabling him to quit
                    the country will be issued to Frank L. Ghiloni, by American authorities within
                    the duration of the present war.</p>
            </div>
